  "question": {
    "text": "A square, of each side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, lies above the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and has one vertex at the origin. If one of the sides passing through the origin makes an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the positive direction of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis&nbsp;, then the sum of the <math><mi>x</mi></math>-coordinates of the vertices of the square is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo></math>"
  },
